  "document": "Marie of Artois\nMarie of Artois (French: Marie d'Artois, Dutch: Maria van Artesië.) Born in 1291, was the fourth daughter of Philip of Artois and Blanche of Brittany. She became the Lady of Méraude (Merode) when she purchased it from John the Blind, King of Bohemia, in 1342."
